STEP 1: Container writable layer is lost on restart
---------------------------------------------------
k run nostore --image=busybox:1.36 -- sh -c "echo hi > /data.txt; sleep 3600"
k exec nostore -- cat /data.txt
Kill the container (not the pod):
  k exec nostore -- kill 1
  k get pod nostore             # RESTARTS 1
  k exec nostore -- cat /data.txt
The file is back only because the command recreates it. Try:
  k exec nostore -- sh -c "echo extra > /extra.txt"
  k exec nostore -- kill 1 ; sleep 5
  k exec nostore -- cat /extra.txt      # gone
k delete pod nostore


STEP 2: emptyDir survives container restarts
--------------------------------------------
vi pod-emptydir.yaml

apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: ed
spec:
  containers:
  - name: writer
    image: busybox:1.36
    command: ["sh", "-c", "while true; do date >> /work/log.txt; sleep 5; done"]
    volumeMounts:
    - name: work
      mountPath: /work
  - name: reader
    image: busybox:1.36
    command: ["sh", "-c", "sleep 3600"]
    volumeMounts:
    - name: work
      mountPath: /data
      readOnly: true
  volumes:
  - name: work
    emptyDir:
      sizeLimit: 100Mi

k apply -f pod-emptydir.yaml
sleep 20
k exec ed -c reader -- cat /data/log.txt
k exec ed -c writer -- kill 1          # restart writer container
sleep 10
k exec ed -c reader -- wc -l /data/log.txt      # old lines still there

Delete the pod and recreate:
  k delete pod ed && k apply -f pod-emptydir.yaml && sleep 10
  k exec ed -c reader -- wc -l /data/log.txt    # starts from zero


